sections.content:
Nakon psalma Vladimir Grebenar dovršava svjedočanstvo s jutarnje molitve. „Vidio sam anđela Gospodnjeg, jednog od te četvorice, kako je pustio iz svoje ruke nešto da se krenu odvijati stvari u svijetu“, opisuje. Viđenje ne tumači podrobnije, nego dodaje: „Tko ima uši da čuje, neka čuje kako stoji pisano u Svetom pismu.“

Viđenje zatim povezuje s aktualnim događajima. U trenutku snimanja, ističe, još ne zna kako će se stvari razviti, ali navodi:

- najavljene velike skupove i prosvjede u **Njemačkoj**;
- veliki štrajk u **Italiji**;
- nerede i nemire po europskim gradovima.

Voditelj se poziva i na ono što je, kako kaže, vidio u molitvi prije nekoliko mjeseci: da će se broj gradova zahvaćenih nemirima povećavati, da će neredi „eruptirati“ te da ih politički lideri i vlade zapadnog svijeta više neće uspjeti spriječiti.

sections.content_en:
After the psalm, Vladimir Grebenar finishes the testimony from the morning prayer. „I saw an angel of the Lord, one of those four, releasing something from his hand for things to start unfolding in the world“, he describes. He does not interpret the vision in more detail, but adds: „He who has ears to hear, let him hear as it stands written in Sacred Scripture.“

He then connects the vision to current events. At the moment of recording, he stresses, he does not yet know how things will develop, but lists:

- announced large gatherings and protests in **Germany**;
- a large strike in **Italy**;
- riots and unrest across European cities.

The host also refers to what he says he saw in prayer several months earlier: that the number of cities gripped by unrest would increase, that riots would „erupt“, and that political leaders and governments of the Western world would no longer succeed in preventing them.

sections.content:
Svetkovinu Svih svetih Vladimir Grebenar naziva **„jako velikom svetkovinom“**, štoviše „svetkovinom Crkve“, te objašnjava po čemu se razlikuje od drugih velikih blagdana:

- na **Uskrs i Božić** u prvom je planu Isus;
- na **Veliku Gospu** u prvom je planu Blažena Djevica Marija;
- na **Duhove** u prvom je planu Duh Sveti.

Isus i Duh Sveti božanske su osobe, a Bogorodica je Majka Božja, koju je Bog podigao da bude Kraljica neba i zemlje, iznad svih stvorenja.

Na svetkovinu Svih svetih, nasuprot tome, slavi se, kako kaže voditelj, „ono čemu mi težimo“, oni koji sada hodaju zemljom. Vjernici teže tome da budu u skupini svih svetih, a to je, naglašava, **Crkva**. Isus, Marija i Duh Sveti glava su Crkve, dok su udovi Crkve svi koji se na zemlji zauzimaju za kraljevstvo Božje i svi koji su umrli i postigli spasenje. Upravo zato je riječ o svetkovini **zajedništva svih svetih**, a voditelj poziva na molitvu za milost da i slušatelji postignu svetost.

sections.content_en:
Vladimir Grebenar calls the solemnity of All Saints a **„very great solemnity“**, moreover a „solemnity of the Church“, and explains how it differs from other major feasts:

- on **Easter and Christmas** Jesus is in the foreground;
- on the **Assumption** the Blessed Virgin Mary is in the foreground;
- on **Pentecost** the Holy Spirit is in the foreground.

Jesus and the Holy Spirit are divine persons, and the Mother of God is the Mother of God, whom God raised up to be Queen of heaven and earth, above all creatures.

On the solemnity of All Saints, in contrast, what is celebrated, as the host says, is „that toward which we strive“, those who now walk the earth. Believers strive to be in the group of all the saints, and that, he emphasizes, is the **Church**. Jesus, Mary, and the Holy Spirit are the head of the Church, while the members of the Church are all who on earth advocate for the kingdom of God and all who have died and attained salvation. That is precisely why this is a solemnity of the **communion of all saints**, and the host calls for prayer for the grace that listeners too may attain holiness.

sections.content:
U posljednjem dijelu emisije Vladimir Grebenar poziva gledatelje i slušatelje da postanu članovi **domoljubne inicijative Ora et Labora** prijavom putem web-stranice. Za otvorena pitanja dostupni su i brojevi mobitela. Zahvaljuje svima koji doniraju i podržavaju rad inicijative.

Zatim se, kako kaže „potpuno otvoreno“ i da „ne bi bilo neke zabune“, osvrće na kritike. Postoje, tvrdi, ljudi koji su „baš jako zločesti, zlonamjerni“ i koji svašta govore i pišu. Odgovara im jasno:

- **ni jedan cent** od donacija nije uzeo za sebe;
- sve donacije nalaze se na računu inicijative i troše se za njezine potrebe;
- njegova je uloga **volonterska**;
- na putovanja ide privatnim automobilom, gorivo plaća sam, a sam plaća i smještaj.

Klevetnike opisuje kao ljude preko kojih djeluje Sotona: „Vrte se unutra, iznutra, prave se da su neki vjernici, katolici“ i šire klevete. Slušateljima poručuje da takvima slobodno mogu odgovoriti da je riječ o kleveti.

Voditelj kaže da je sve to „u ime Isusovo otresao sa sebe“ i da to ne želi trpjeti. Već dovoljno trpi, objašnjava, zbog evangelizacije i zbog desetaka tisuća ljudi koji rastu u vjeri, što sve osjeća „na svojim leđima“. Prozivke da sebi isplaćuje novac namijenjen širenju kraljevstva Božjega na zemlji naziva „strašnim klevetama“.

„Ne bih bio u koži tim ljudima“, dodaje. Kaže da ih je predao Gospodinu i od njega zazvao zaštitu, pozivajući se na evanđeoske riječi o nagodbi s protivnikom dok se još na putu, da ga ne preda sucu. Klevetnike je, kako kaže, „predao sucu Gospodinu“.

Na kraju moli slušatelje da budu „široke ruke i otvorena srca“. Novac, naglašava, nije potreban za privatne potrebe, nego za provedbu projekata „koji su za Gospodina“. Kao primjer navodi portal **ohl.hr**, na kojem rade novinari kojima treba isplatiti plaće. Dodaje da to danas više neće ponavljati, ali da će se, bude li potrebno, tome povremeno vraćati. „Ja sam ovdje slobodan od svega toga“, zaključuje.

sections.content_en:
In the final part of the program, Vladimir Grebenar invites viewers and listeners to become members of the **patriotic initiative Ora et Labora** by registering via the website. Mobile phone numbers are also available for open questions. He thanks everyone who donates and supports the initiative's work.

Then, as he says „completely openly“ and so that „there would be no confusion“, he addresses the criticisms. There are, he claims, people who are „really very wicked, malicious“ and who say and write all kinds of things. He answers them clearly:

- he has not taken **a single cent** of donations for himself;
- all donations are in the initiative's account and are spent on its needs;
- his role is **voluntary**;
- he travels by private car, pays for fuel himself, and pays for accommodation himself.

He describes slanderers as people through whom Satan operates: „They circle inside, from within, pretending to be some kind of believers, Catholics“ and spread slander. He tells listeners that they are free to reply to such people that it is slander.

The host says that he has „in the name of Jesus shaken this off himself“ and that he does not want to endure it. He already endures enough, he explains, because of evangelization and because of tens of thousands of people growing in faith, all of which he feels „on his back“. He calls allegations that he pays himself money intended for spreading the kingdom of God on earth „terrible slanders“.

„I wouldn't want to be in those people's shoes“, he adds. He says he has handed them over to the Lord and invoked protection from Him, referring to the gospel words about settling with an opponent while still on the way, lest he hand one over to the judge. He has, as he says, „handed the slanderers over to the judge, the Lord“.

In the end he asks listeners to be „generous and open-hearted“. Money, he emphasizes, is not needed for private needs, but for the implementation of projects „that are for the Lord“. As an example he cites the portal **ohl.hr**, where journalists work who need to be paid salaries. He adds that he will not repeat this today anymore, but that, if necessary, he will return to it periodically. „I am free of all that here“, he concludes.
